1
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:11,670
Morning's here

2
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:14,090
The morning's here

3
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:16,680
Sunshine is here

4
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:18,300
The sky is clear

5
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:22,270
The morning's here

6
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:23,770
Hey!

7
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:28,520
Do you have to do that? It's Saturday!

8
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,520
Oh, come on!

9
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:32,440
Morning's here!

10
00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:36,160
Morning's here

11
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:38,530
The morning's here

12
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,580
Sunshine is here

13
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:46,420
I hate this apartment!

14
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:52,090
I hate the color of these walls! I hate that this place still smells like bird!

15
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,010
I hate that singing guy!

16
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:59,600
Are you kidding? I love that guy!

17
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:03,180
Morning's here, morning is...

18
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:05,140
Stop it!

19
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:07,560
I will kill you.

20
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:12,730
I hate that my room is so small.

21
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:15,610
I have all the space I need. Just do what I did.

22
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:19,660
Monica, you don't even have a bed. You sleep in a ball on the floor!

23
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:23,740
You know what? I am tired of your bellyaching.

24
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:27,250
I've worked really hard at making this a nice place for us to live.

25
00:01:27,830 --> 00:01:29,710
I know. I'm so sorry.

26
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,750
I'm sorry, okay?

27
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:33,250
This is a great apartment.

28
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:35,340
Shut up. This place is a hole.

29
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:34,150
Oh, blimey, I still can't believe you've got an earring!

30
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:37,400
I know, I know. Who am I? David Bowie?

31
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:40,820
He does that?

32
00:02:40,990 --> 00:02:43,070
I don't know. Whatever.

33
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:46,290
Well, I think it makes you look really dangerous.

34
00:02:46,450 --> 00:02:48,750
Oh, I know.

35
00:02:49,330 --> 00:02:50,540
You know what?

36
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:53,540
I never would've gotten this if it weren't for you.

37
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:57,250
No, really. When I'm with you, I'm like...

38
00:02:57,420 --> 00:03:00,170
...this whole other guy. I love that guy!

39
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,510
I mean, I love you too. A lot.

40
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,930
But that guy!

41
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:06,510
I love that guy!

42
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:08,520
I love both of you.

43
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,690
I wish I didn't have to go.

44
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,770
Then don't.

45
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:18,650
Stay here. Don't go so soon to London.

46
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,190
- Just one more day.     - Oh, Ross.

47
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,610
- One more day.     - Please don't do this to me again.

48
00:03:23,490 --> 00:03:27,490
You know I'd stay, but I've already missed so much work. They'll fire me.

49
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:30,870
So? Then you could stay as long as you want.

50
00:03:31,830 --> 00:03:33,290
I wish I could.

51
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,460
Oh, no, don't... Don't... Don't start packing.

52
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:39,420
Come on.

53
00:03:42,090 --> 00:03:43,970
I don't think you understand packing.

54
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:48,100
I don't want to leave it till the last minute.

55
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:50,890
Last time I packed in a rush, I left my knickers here.

56
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,980
Yeah, I know. I, uh, tried them on.

57
00:03:54,650 --> 00:03:56,020
You didn't!

58
00:03:56,190 --> 00:03:58,730
No, I didn't. I didn't want to be "that guy."

59
00:04:07,910 --> 00:04:09,450
Hello.

60
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:12,290
Ho, ho, ho.

61
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,420
- Excuse me?     - Your pants.

62
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,840
Oh, yeah! You like them?

63
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,460
I went to a used-clothes store and got maternity stuff.

64
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:25,510
These are so comfortable.

65
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:31,600
Uh, Pheebs, those are, uh, Santa pants.

66
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,890
- What?     - Santa pants.

67
00:04:35,850 --> 00:04:37,600
Santa Claus' pants.

68
00:04:39,190 --> 00:04:41,440
Nuh-uh. They're maternity pants.

69
00:04:41,610 --> 00:04:44,990
They even came with a list of baby names. See?

70
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:48,240
These names are good, and these are bad.

71
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:54,580
- Hey!     - Hey.

72
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:56,040
Hey, Pheebs.

73
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:58,880
So, how are the elves?

74
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:04,380
I don't know. How are the, uh, you know?

75
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:08,010
Your clothes aren't funny.

76
00:05:09,550 --> 00:05:12,140
Hey, guys, what should I wear to a Knicks game?

77
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:15,140
Uh, a T-shirt that says, "I Don't Belong Here"?

78
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,480
You have tickets?

79
00:05:18,650 --> 00:05:23,030
Mom got Dad's season tickets in the divorce, so she gave them to me.

80
00:05:23,190 --> 00:05:25,400
Apparently, they're good seats.

81
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:27,950
Oh, my God! Those are almost on the floor!

82
00:05:28,110 --> 00:05:29,820
Do you guys want these?

83
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:32,370
- Yeah!     - Yeah, we do!

84
00:05:32,910 --> 00:05:34,290
Well, you got them!

85
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:36,660
- All right!     - Just give us our apartment back.

86
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:42,710
Whoa, I didn't see that coming.

87
00:05:44,590 --> 00:05:45,630
Are you serious?

88
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:49,590
Come on. We know what these are worth.

89
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:51,850
Do you think we're stupid?

90
00:05:52,010 --> 00:05:55,390
Not stupid. You're meaner than I thought.

91
00:05:56,390 --> 00:05:57,930
- What do you say?     - Forget it.

92
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:02,020
Okay? I'm not giving up my bachelor pad for basketball seats.

93
00:06:02,190 --> 00:06:04,610
Your "bachelor pad"?

94
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,780
Have you even had a girl here?

95
00:06:09,450 --> 00:06:10,950
No.

96
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:15,200
But Joey has, and I usually talk to them in the morning time.

97
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:19,160
Yeah, you do.

98
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:26,880
Come on!

99
00:06:27,050 --> 00:06:30,220
Gunther, can I get two cups of chino, please?

100
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:31,800
Good one.

101
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:34,680
Come on. Season tickets.

102
00:06:34,850 --> 00:06:37,060
Season tickets! You know what that means?

103
00:06:37,230 --> 00:06:39,270
Forget it. I'm not giving up the apartment.

104
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:43,190
When I was a kid, my dad's company gave season tickets...

105
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:48,280
...to the Number 1 salesman every year. All right? My dad never won.

106
00:06:48,690 --> 00:06:52,610
Of course, he wasn't in sales. But still, I never forgot that!

107
00:06:53,910 --> 00:06:55,780
- Hey guys!     - Hey.

108
00:06:57,410 --> 00:06:59,120
Oh, my God.

109
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:02,210
We don't make enough fun of you already?

110
00:07:03,290 --> 00:07:05,750
Oh, yeah. Emily convinced me to do it.

111
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:09,090
You do know that Wham broke up?

112
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:15,510
I like it. And Emily likes it. And that's what counts.

113
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,720
So, uh, how are you guys doing?

114
00:07:19,890 --> 00:07:23,310
Don't try and talk all normal with that thing in your ear.

115
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,860
Where's Emily?

116
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:28,190
Ugh, she's saying goodbye to her uncle.

117
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:32,070
- Didn't she, like, just get here?     - Yeah! Yeah.

118
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,410
Easy, tiger.

119
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:36,030
I just hate this so much.

120
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:40,120
Every time I go pick her up at the airport, it's so great.

121
00:07:40,290 --> 00:07:45,130
But I'm thinking, "I'll be right back in a couple of days, dropping her off."

122
00:07:45,290 --> 00:07:47,880
- So, what'll you do?     - There's nothing to do.

123
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:49,750
She lives there. I live here.

124
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:52,590
She'd have to move here.

125
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:54,470
She should move here.

126
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:56,470
What?

127
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:59,140
- I can ask her to live with me.     - Are you serious?

128
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:02,560
- Why not? I mean, why not?     - You've only known her six weeks!

129
00:08:02,730 --> 00:08:06,770
I've got a carton of milk in my fridge I've had a longer relationship with.

130
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:11,030
Look, guys, when I'm with her, it's like...

131
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:15,030
Uh, she brings out this great side of me.

132
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,620
I mean, I love her, you know?

133
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:19,740
And I love the milk!

134
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:23,870
But I won't ask some British girl to move in with me.

135
00:08:28,590 --> 00:08:30,800
Joey, you say things now.

136
00:08:32,010 --> 00:08:34,800
Look, Ross. He's right. Emily's great.

137
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:36,260
She's great!

138
00:08:36,430 --> 00:08:39,180
But this is too soon. You're only gonna scare her.

139
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:41,520
- I don't wanna do that.     - No.

140
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:44,810
You don't want to wreck it. Don't go too fast.

141
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:47,650
No. You're right. I know, you're right.

142
00:08:47,810 --> 00:08:49,650
I'm not going to do it.

143
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:53,360
- Thanks guys.     - No problem.

144
00:08:53,530 --> 00:08:55,820
Just remember to wake us up before you go-go.

145
00:09:07,170 --> 00:09:09,920
It's too hard. Too hard!

146
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:13,670
All right, boys. Last chance for the tickets.

147
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:17,430
Otherwise, I give them to my new boyfriend, Joshua.

148
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:20,640
No, thank you.

149
00:09:21,010 --> 00:09:24,220
Wait, wait. Come on, come on! Let's trade.

150
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:26,850
The timing's perfect! I just clogged the toilet!

151
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:34,030
I want those seats as much as you. But we can't live in the small apartment...

152
00:09:34,190 --> 00:09:37,110
...after we've lived here! Ever read Flowers for Algernon?

153
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:38,990
Yes.

154
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,070
Ever read Sports Illustrated?

155
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:45,160
No, I didn't read yours!

156
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:46,910
We can go to the game tonight!

157
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:49,670
The only way I'll consider this...

158
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:52,130
...is if they offer more than just season seats.

159
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,750
- It's the Knicks!     - Screw the Knicks.

160
00:10:00,010 --> 00:10:02,600
I didn't mean that. I just meant...

161
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:05,770
...that the apartment is worth so much more.

162
00:10:09,770 --> 00:10:10,980
And the Knicks rule all.

163
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:12,610
Yeah, the Knicks rule all!

164
00:10:14,110 --> 00:10:15,940
Hey, so? Are you going to do it?

165
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:20,410
No, we're not going to because it's not an even trade.

166
00:10:20,570 --> 00:10:21,700
All right, look.

167
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:24,910
What if you could keep the apartment and the tickets?

168
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,120
Done!

169
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:30,290
Let me finish. I'm talking about a bet. Winner takes all.

170
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:31,710
Ooh, we could get nothing.

171
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:34,790
- Or you can end up with everything.     - Oh, I like that.

172
00:10:36,420 --> 00:10:37,510
What do you say?

173
00:10:37,670 --> 00:10:39,510
- No!     - Just do it!

174
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,300
Oh! Oh, I'm convinced!

175
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:46,640
Come on, man! You know I'd do it for you.

176
00:10:46,810 --> 00:10:49,140
Because you're my best friend.

177
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:53,560
All right. But you can't use that again for a whole year.

178
00:10:54,400 --> 00:10:55,440
I'm in.

179
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:59,570
This is so exciting! What are you going to bet?

180
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:01,780
Okay. Well, we should let Phoebe decide...

181
00:11:01,990 --> 00:11:06,030
...because she's the only one who's impartial, and she's so pretty.

182
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:09,160
Okay. Ha, ha. Um...

183
00:11:09,330 --> 00:11:11,370
Ooh, ooh. Oh, I have a game!

184
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:14,170
- This is great!     - Okay. What's the game?

185
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:17,750
Um, well, it doesn't have a name. No, okay. Phoebe Ball!

186
00:11:19,590 --> 00:11:22,220
No, it doesn't have a name. Um...

187
00:11:22,430 --> 00:11:24,470
Okay, Monica.

188
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:28,390
What is your favorite thing about trees?

189
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:32,850
- They're green?     - Good! Good, five points!

190
00:11:37,270 --> 00:11:39,230
All right, Joey...

191
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:41,320
Same question.

192
00:11:43,950 --> 00:11:46,870
- Oh! Heh. They're tall.     - Ooh, three points.

193
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:53,960
Both fine answers, but we were looking for leafy. Leafy.

194
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:57,710
That's not even a game.

195
00:11:57,880 --> 00:11:59,960
Shut up. We're winning!

196
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:04,340
You want to finish this? We get a deck of cards.

197
00:12:04,510 --> 00:12:06,220
High card wins. What do you say?

198
00:12:06,390 --> 00:12:08,300
- Let's do it!     - Oh, I have cards!

199
00:12:08,470 --> 00:12:10,470
- Oh, good.     - Yeah. Here.

200
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,140
No, these are the trick deck.

201
00:12:12,310 --> 00:12:14,640
Okay. Here, yes.

202
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:17,400
Okay, you guys, uh, you pick first.

203
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:19,020
- Okay.     - Okay?

204
00:12:22,860 --> 00:12:24,780
- Four.     - That's a low one!

205
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:30,290
Phoebe, you look. I can't do it.

206
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:33,330
- What makes you think I can?     - That's okay.

207
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,500
Ace!

208
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:41,000
Why are you hugging?

209
00:12:41,170 --> 00:12:42,920
Because we won our apartment back!

210
00:12:43,090 --> 00:12:46,260
What? Ace is high! Jack, queen, king, ace!

211
00:12:46,430 --> 00:12:49,180
No! Ace is low! Ace, two, three, four!

212
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:58,270
I don't know.

213
00:13:02,030 --> 00:13:04,070
Look it! Aah!

214
00:13:06,570 --> 00:13:09,240
- All right, come on, pick again!     - Okay, give me.

215
00:13:09,410 --> 00:13:11,160
- Okay.     - Okay.

216
00:13:11,330 --> 00:13:13,950
Come on, apartment! Come on, apartment!

217
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:19,580
Aah! I know queen is high!

218
00:13:19,750 --> 00:13:21,170
Not as high as...

219
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:23,800
It worked! King!

220
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:28,930
We pick again! We pick again!

221
00:13:29,090 --> 00:13:30,600
- Why?     - I don't know.

222
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:35,270
Tickets, please.

223
00:13:36,350 --> 00:13:39,310
That's courtside, baby!

224
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:42,230
Seriously, good game, though. Good game.

225
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:47,450
What are they so mad about? They got the apartment back.

226
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:49,610
No, they didn't.

227
00:14:00,210 --> 00:14:02,000
Packed while you were gone.

228
00:14:02,210 --> 00:14:04,630
I left some knickers under your pillow.

229
00:14:06,590 --> 00:14:08,170
Move in with me.

230
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:09,880
What?

231
00:14:10,050 --> 00:14:14,760
Don't be scared. It sounds crazy, and people will say it's too soon...

232
00:14:14,930 --> 00:14:19,810
...but just think. Think how great it would be.

233
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,980
I don't know.

234
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:27,690
Uh, oh, leaving London.

235
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:29,780
- My whole family lives there...     - I know.

236
00:14:29,950 --> 00:14:32,910
- My job.     - You'll get a job here.

237
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:37,120
I always hear about them foreigners stealing American jobs.

238
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:39,330
That could be you.

239
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:42,130
Yeah, but it's my whole life.

240
00:14:42,630 --> 00:14:43,880
You come to England.

241
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:47,090
I can't. I would. I really would. But my son is here.

242
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:51,260
I can't leave him. You don't think there's any way?

243
00:14:52,470 --> 00:14:54,260
Oh, I don't think so.

244
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:59,270
It would be different if it was way into the future...

245
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,940
...and we were getting married or something.

246
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:03,190
What?

247
00:15:03,650 --> 00:15:07,150
Uh, no, right. I shouldn't have said "married."

248
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:09,030
Uh, please don't go freaky on me.

249
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:12,610
I didn't mean it. I didn't say it. I take it back.

250
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:14,120
No. Don't.

251
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:18,290
Why don't we?

252
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:20,500
Why don't we what?

253
00:15:22,370 --> 00:15:24,000
Get married.

254
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,540
You are mad!

255
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:31,630
No, I'm not! It's perfect. It's better than you moving here.

256
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:34,930
It's us together forever, and that's what I want.

257
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,680
- We've known each other six weeks!     - Yeah, I know.

258
00:15:37,850 --> 00:15:41,640
So what? Who's to say? Does that mean we can't do it?

259
00:15:41,810 --> 00:15:46,020
Look. I was with Carol for four years before we got married...

260
00:15:46,190 --> 00:15:49,440
...and I wound up divorced from a pregnant lesbian.

261
00:15:51,860 --> 00:15:53,400
I mean, this...

262
00:15:54,110 --> 00:15:56,530
This makes sense for us.

263
00:15:57,910 --> 00:16:02,330
Come on. Our first date, we ended up spending the whole weekend in Vermont.

264
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:05,710
I mean, last night I got my ear pierced. Me!

265
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:08,960
This feels right.

266
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:10,880
Doesn't it?

267
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:15,010
My parents are gonna be really mad.

268
00:16:15,390 --> 00:16:17,970
Is that...? Are you saying "Yes"? Is that "Yes"?

269
00:16:19,060 --> 00:16:20,390
Yes.

270
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,600
- Yes!     - Yes?

271
00:16:24,770 --> 00:16:26,940
- We're getting married!     - Oh, my God!

272
00:16:27,110 --> 00:16:30,400
- Yes! Ha, ha.     - We're getting married!

273
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:32,240
Come here, come here.

274
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:44,160
Emily, will you marry me?

275
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:47,250
Yes.

276
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:52,710
Oh, it's a bit small.

277
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:56,930
Damn! I thought that'd be romantic as hell.

278
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:01,430
It was.

279
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:18,200
- Those were, like, the best seats ever.     - Oh, yeah.

280
00:17:18,410 --> 00:17:21,950
Hey, should we give these to the girls? Like a peace offering?

281
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:25,410
That's very nice. Plus, they were free and too small.

282
00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:32,460
Oh, God.

283
00:17:39,050 --> 00:17:40,510
Hey, you want a beer?

284
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,560
- Whoa!     - I know!

285
00:17:48,850 --> 00:17:51,150
Open up! Open up! Open up!

286
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,570
We'll discuss it in the morning.

287
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,240
What the hell is going on?

288
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:07,910
We took our apartment back!

289
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:13,210
I had nothing to do with it.

290
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:20,300
Okay, it was my idea. But I don't feel good about it.

291
00:18:24,260 --> 00:18:27,100
We are switching back right now.

292
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:29,190
No, we're not. We're not leaving!

293
00:18:29,350 --> 00:18:31,310
You'll have to. You both have jobs.

294
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:35,150
As soon as you do, we're switching back! There's nothing you can do to stop us.

295
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,730
Right, Joe?

296
00:18:36,900 --> 00:18:37,940
I don't know.

297
00:18:41,950 --> 00:18:43,030
What?

298
00:18:43,530 --> 00:18:45,950
I don't want to move again, with...

299
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:50,830
I don't care! This is our apartment and they stole...

300
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,250
You stole!

301
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:56,550
Our apartment! We won it fair and square. Twice!

302
00:18:56,710 --> 00:19:00,550
And I am getting it back right now! I'm getting it back right now!

303
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:03,590
All right.

304
00:19:04,390 --> 00:19:08,850
We figured you might respond this way, so we have a backup offer.

305
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:12,060
Oh, no more offers. You can't offer anything to us!

306
00:19:12,230 --> 00:19:16,610
- Let us keep the apartment and...     - As a thank you...

307
00:19:20,030 --> 00:19:22,410
...Rachel and I will kiss for one minute.

308
00:19:26,740 --> 00:19:29,620
- Totally worth it.     - That was one good minute.

309
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:31,710
- Good night.     - Good night.

310
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:39,420
- Men are such idiots.     - I know.

311
00:19:39,590 --> 00:19:44,260
Can you believe something that stupid actually got us our apartment back?

312
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:47,720
It's funny. If you had just done that after the last contest...

313
00:19:47,890 --> 00:19:50,100
...no one would have had to move at all. Ha, ha.

314
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,980
Let's pretend that's not true.

315
00:19:58,110 --> 00:20:00,440
Okay. Scarf's done.

316
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:06,490
- Come on. Come on, come on!     - Okay.

317
00:20:07,450 --> 00:20:08,870
- Hey!     - Hey.

318
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,080
What's going on?

319
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:12,290
Ross has some big thing to tell everyone.

320
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:16,830
Well, okay. It's, uh... Ahem.

321
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,590
Emily and I, we decided to, uh...

322
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,590
...to get married.

323
00:20:24,470 --> 00:20:25,800
- What?     - Oh, my God.

324
00:20:25,970 --> 00:20:28,390
Oh, are you pregnant too?

325
00:20:30,470 --> 00:20:31,930
No.

326
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:35,100
When did...? How did you...?

327
00:20:35,270 --> 00:20:38,150
We just decided to go for it.

328
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:41,480
We know it's a bit hasty, but, uh...

329
00:20:41,650 --> 00:20:43,820
...it just feels so right.

330
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:50,740
Um, I was just telling the guys...

331
00:20:50,910 --> 00:20:53,000
Yeah, I heard.

332
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:01,630
I think it's great! Aah!

333
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,260
I'm so happy for you!

334
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:04,840
Well, yeah! Congratulations!

335
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:16,520
- I can't believe you're getting married!     - Yeah.

336
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:22,610
Monica and Rachel made out.

337
00:21:33,330 --> 00:21:37,290
Morning's here

338
00:21:37,460 --> 00:21:40,130
The morning's here

339
00:21:40,290 --> 00:21:42,840
Sunshine is here

340
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:44,550
The sky is clear

341
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:47,220
The morning's here

342
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:48,590
- Hey, you're back!     - Hey!

343
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:52,760
- Get into gear     - Breakfast is near

344
00:21:52,930 --> 00:21:58,060
The dark of night has disappeared

345
00:21:58,230 --> 00:22:01,770
- I'll see you tomorrow morning!     - Okay!

